{
  "$comment": "AEP-0001 §8.2 down-leveling at a fan-out hop: the rewritten event MUST honor its new capture level (§8.2a — `metadata` means no free text). Cases pin downlevel(): nested annotated fields (answer.text, error.message) are pruned via dotted-path annotations, and the AEP-0002 §5.3 [metadata*] exception fields (prompt / options[].label / field_spec labels / answer.values free text) degrade structurally below `redacted` — a hop has no source context to synthesize or classify, and dropping more than required is always legal (§8.2b). Found by review: before this corpus, a redacted attention.answered down-leveled to a metadata consumer kept answer.text verbatim. Second review finding, §8.2(e): `redacted` is a provenance claim (the free text passed the AEP-0003 §9.4 pipeline) that a mechanical hop can never mint — a `redacted` ceiling on a `full` event rewrites to `metadata` (DL6/DL10/DL11), because redacted-gated fields at capture:full may be verbatim (AEP-0002 §5.1 r2) and would otherwise ride relabeled as redacted; a redacted-SOURCE event passes a redacted ceiling unchanged (DL12 — the claim was minted at source). Consumed by BOTH runners: run.js exercises the shared JS implementation the relay uses; run.py holds its own independent implementation written from the spec text.",
